Storage behavior:
- If served over http/https, submit to API route /api/wishes using FormData.
- If API is unavailable or page is opened directly from file, save fallback locally in localStorage.
- Merge database wishes with local wishes.
- Show latest wishes first.
- Clear saved wishes button clears database if available and localStorage.

Wish card behavior:
- Each wish card shows optional photo, sender name, message, good-deed text, date.
- Add a button: "Read & thank".
- Clicking the button uses speech synthesis to read:
  "{name} sent this birthday wish: {message}. Good deed shared: {deed}. Thank you, {name}, from Vidyadhar Navath, for sending your wishes, blessings, and good-deed memories. Your message means a lot."
- If no deed exists, omit the deed sentence.
- Use an Indian English female voice if available; otherwise use available speech synthesis voice.
- Update form note while reading.

Database model:
- Use separate stores/files/tables for login accounts and wishes.
- Wishes store should never contain password fields.
- Login store should never be exposed to client except public user id/name/createdAt.
- Passwords must be hashed with salt. Never store raw passwords.
- Do not return email to browser storage unless explicitly required.
- For production hosting, use a real persistent database such as Supabase, Neon Postgres, MongoDB Atlas, or Vercel Postgres.
- File JSON is acceptable only for local development.

